{"_id":"68a7363c8ec3d8323af1f09a","nodeId":"ddtVaA4Ls6qRj-7OtTSIH","roadmapSlug":"sql","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:40.099Z","description":"# DELETE Statement\n\nThe DELETE statement removes rows from a table. You specify which table to remove data from and can use a WHERE clause to filter which rows should be deleted based on specific conditions. If no WHERE clause is provided, all rows in the table will be deleted.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"DELETE","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/sql/sql_delete.asp","_id":"69bba6b933a0ad7a57afe68b"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-19T07:33:13.507Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d0416838","title":"DataCamp - SQL Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/ZVeXng"},{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d04167c7","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/sql/content/ddtVaA4Ls6qRj-7OtTSIH.md"}